{"nodes": [{"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_ipc_protocol", "label": "Chrono::ROS internal IPC protocol", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Documented not because users need it - handlers and the message API hide it entirely - but for debugging the bridge, porting to a new ROS 2 distribution, or understanding how messages cross the process boundary."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_chrono_ros_node", "label": "chrono_ros_node subprocess", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Strict symbol separation: the simulation process contains no ROS symbols and the subprocess contains no Chrono physics symbols, joined by a bidirectional shared-memory channel. The subprocess uses rclcpp generic publishers/subscriptions with introspection type support so it never needs compiled message types."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_frames", "label": "IPC frame kinds", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fixed frame set (HELLO, DESCRIBE_TYPE, TYPE_SCHEMA, VALIDATE_TYPE, VALIDATE_RESULT, ADVERTISE, ADVERTISE_ACK, PUBLISH, RECEIVED, UNADVERTISE, CHANNEL_INFO, SHUTDOWN), each a header of magic, protocol version, kind, channel_id, sim_time_ns and payload_size followed by its payload."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_channel_info", "label": "CHANNEL_INFO subscriber counting", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Carries live subscriber/publisher counts updated as the ROS graph changes; this is the mechanism behind ChROSPublisher::GetSubscriptionCount() and therefore behind a handler skipping work when nobody is listening."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_runtime_schema_blob", "label": "Runtime type schema blob", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The simulation process never parses .msg files. On first use of a type it sends DESCRIBE_TYPE; the subprocess resolves the name through the sourced ROS environment, walks rosidl introspection type support recursively, and returns a packed schema blob from which the bridge builds its serializer and deserializer - which is why any installed message type, custom packages included, works by name with no code in Chrono. The blob stays a simple versioned packed little-endian format because both ends are built from the same source tree and it never crosses a version boundary."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_cdr_encoding", "label": "XCDR1 plain-CDR encoding", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The payload crossing the channel is the ROS message serialized as CDR - the same bytes ROS 2 puts on the wire - encoded by a small dependency-free codec in the simulation process. XCDR1 is sufficient because all ROS 2 message types are @final and are serialized as plain CDR by both rmw_fastrtps and rmw_cyclonedds."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_type_validation", "label": "Per-type run-time codec validation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The codec is verified per type at run time rather than trusted by assertion: at Initialize() the bridge sends a canonical test-pattern message via VALIDATE_TYPE, the subprocess round-trips it through rclcpp serialization and byte-compares, so a mismatch (e.g. a future rmw switching to XCDR2) aborts Initialize() with a precise error instead of publishing corrupt data. Implementation note: rmw serializers do not guarantee interior padding bytes, so the node zero-fills its re-serialization buffer to keep skipped padding from being reported as field mismatches."}], "edges": [{"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_ipc_protocol", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_chrono_ros_node", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_ipc_protocol", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_frames", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_ipc_protocol", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_channel_info", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_ipc_protocol", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_runtime_schema_blob", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_ipc_protocol", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_cdr_encoding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_ipc_protocol", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_type_validation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_ipc_protocol", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_chroshandler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_channel_info", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_chrospublisher", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_runtime_schema_blob", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_frames", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/ipc_protocol.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_runtime_schema_blob", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ipc_protocol_cdr_encoding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED"